2491-- The [trace review](research/2026-10-26-thesis-admission-v12/trace-review.md) reads every thesis, every gold failure and the duplicate aggregates to their raw requests, answers and matching decisions, and names the root causes by design layer: thesis identity is a quantity where the analyst's unit is a question (six 2026 aggregates, each judged "new" correctly under the current criterion); the contract under-produces on first contact with a company (AMD 2 theses, MSFT 0); the role states categories where the labeller applies tests; theme candidates name no dependant; the extractor never sees the current view. Six general mechanisms are proposed with the class and count each moves, in the order: matching's "another estimate or population of the same question" option and theme dependants (code and schema, no prompt growth), then role v13 (tests instead of lists, the first-contact rule, quarterly statements as evidence; net shorter), then showing the view in block 5 as an A/B, then the daily duplicate check as pull-mode design. Each is Alex's call; none is built here.
