2493-## D190 · 2026-10-26 · The collision judge: Jev for identity, the generative model for the analyst's question when a question may be held twice
2494-
2495-- Alex: "查重是用的 Jev 吗？… 你可以先单独跑这个，重新 review 一次 Jev 的提示词，然后优化他，不仅达到你的目的，也更贴近 hedge fund analyst 的大脑，你有黄金集做标准". Jev answers every candidate-to-thesis relation and every evidence comparison since D169.
2496-- Review of Jev's relation criteria against the r3 ledger ([probe](../poc/reports/2026-10-26-admission-v12/jev-relation-probe/probe.md), 31 stored candidate calls whose list holds a thesis of the same object and measure, 18 labelled by the assistant): under the current options Jev calls a population variant of one aggregate `part_of` (0.4–0.9) and the code maps that to "new"; under an analyst's option set ("one question: the same outcome settles both; another estimate, population or proxy of one aggregate is the same question") it answers `distinct_question_same_matter` 0.5–0.9 on the same pairs. Both wordings: 8 of 18 right. Jev compares wording; it does not hold the decision. No change to Jev's criteria is made: the measured criteria stay (D167–D169).
2497-- The generative model asked the same analyst question on the same 18 ([records](../poc/reports/2026-10-26-admission-v12/jev-relation-probe/llm-records.json), 3 samples each, $0.02): 11 of 18 right by majority, and 5 of the 6 aggregate duplicates merged; the misses are the debatable pairs (a reporting segment beside the business segment, the same deal under two names).
2498-- Decided to build and run alone: `matching` keeps Jev; a configuration may add a `collision` setting (model, prompt `collision-v1`). When a candidate's list holds a thesis of its own object and measure, one generative call answers the analyst question for those theses and its verdict replaces Jev's on them (`jev_matching.collision_peers`, `ask_collision_judge`); every other relation stays Jev's. `poc-v26` = `poc-v25` plus the judge. Measured by one run over seed, week and August against the extraction gold and the census (ledger `english-v26-collision-r4-2026-10-26`); result appended here.
2499-- General, not a list: the routing rule is a structural fact of the library (two theses of one object and quantity), and the question is the one a desk asks. The cost is one call per collision (31 of 69 candidates on r3), about $0.002 each.
2500-- Result (run r4, `poc-v26`, seed + week + August, $1.33): 26 collision verdicts, 9 merges or successions, all on aggregate variants; 2026 aggregate theses 6 → 2 (v23: 11); theses 60 → 45; no merge removed a thesis the gold wants and A17 (the four-company figure as evidence to the five-company aggregate) turns full. The gold's overall score moved 9 → 4 full, and every lost case is an extraction difference between two fresh runs of the same v12 prompt (Rubin not opened from the call this time, the NAVER and META lines not extracted), not a matching decision. Recorded as the measurement rule for later arms: a matching change is judged on stored candidates and the duplicate census; an extraction change needs three fresh runs or pinned extraction answers; a one-run gold score carries about ±5 cases of sampler noise on this corpus. `poc-v25` stays the replay default until the judge is measured that way.
2501-- Confirmation with extraction pinned (same recorded extraction answers in both arms, ids translated, Jev live, judging synthetic; `pinned_matching_study.py`): control reproduces r3 (60 theses, gold 9 full); the judge arm 56 theses, 2026 aggregates 6 → 3, evidence equal (711 vs 707 rows), gold 8 full with the one difference a repeat the scorer cannot see; 31 verdicts, 6 merges, $0.011; no required thesis lost. Alex: "有效果我们可以做". `poc-v26` becomes the replay default; `poc-v25` stays as a configuration. Open: the judge leaves 2 of 5 aggregate duplicates apart on one sample; a majority of three samples on collisions would cost three cents a run.
