2505-- On the theme-dependency design (`docs/research/2026-10-26-theme-dependencies/design.md`), Alex decided the four points:
2506-  1. A theme candidate does **not** have to name the company thesis it feeds. Alex: "我觉得这个非常难，有时候一个政策影响非常的广，你这种做法基本不可行，不可能所有的公司都 map 到，你可以默认这些宏观的东西和所有公司都有影响，我觉得这个 1 to all mapping 比较 make sense，至于这个 thesis 的 state 对每个不同公司的影响需要别的方法来判断". Decided: a theme thesis is context for every company thesis (one to all); how its state bears on each company is decided when that company's thesis is judged, not by an edge written at extraction. Explicit dependencies stay for the cases a document states (a company thesis on another thesis), and may be added to an existing thesis later (point 2).
2507-  2. A dependency may be added to an existing thesis by a later item ("可以").
